Verify_ParExpansionOff_Enabling_Disabling_RMOD_Energy_Saving
    [Documentation]
    ...  The purpose of this test case is to verify energy saving feature activation through checking of voltage and power values readed on RMOD.
    ...  Feature introduces a new parameter: ParExpansionOff, which can enable or disable the Peak to Average Ratio (PAR) Expansion range
    ...  for Airscale FDD Radios to gain better energy efficiency. It allows for power saving of up to 10% of the PA power consumption without
    ...  having a significant throughput degradation.
    ...
    ...  ARGS:
    ...  :param int rmod_id: (Mandatory): config RMOD ID of tested radio module, e.g.: 1
    ...  :param int nr_cell_id: (Mandatory if lte_cell_id not set): global cell ID of NR cell commissioned on tested radio module, used to emulate
    ...                                                             data transfer, e.g.: 1
    ...                                                             Defaults to None means cell will not be used during measurements.
    ...  :param int lte_cell_id: (Mandatory if nr_cell_id not set): global cell ID of LTE cell commissioned on tested radio module, used to emulate
    ...                                                             data transfer, e.g.: 11
    ...                                                             Defaults to None means cell will not be used during measurements.
    ...  :param int ant_tx_id: (Optional): id of antenna tx used by tested cell(s), defaults to 1.
    ...  :param str avg_power_consumption_mesurement_delay: (Optional): delay (in robot time format) before starting measurements of average power consumption,
    ...                                                                 defaults to 2min
    ...  :param str avg_power_consumption_mesurement_timeout: (Optional): duration (in robot time format) of measurements to calculate average power consumption
    ...                                                                   defaults to 5min
    ...  :param str avg_power_consumption_mesurement_interval: (Optional): interval (in robot time format) between measurements to calculate average power consumption
    ...                                                                    defaults to 1min


